WEBVTT

00:03.240 --> 00:04.434
Got your homework done?

00:05.400 --> 00:07.118
- All of it?
- Yep.

00:08.160 --> 00:10.276
Attaboy.
You just get to kick back this weekend.

00:10.440 --> 00:12.237
That's my plan.

00:12.400 --> 00:13.515
Except...?

00:13.960 --> 00:15.154
Except nothing.

00:15.960 --> 00:16.915
Well, excuse me.

00:20.320 --> 00:21.958
- Oh, yeah.
- There it is.

00:24.000 --> 00:26.036
I might have to write
a book report for Monday.

00:26.360 --> 00:28.078
What do you mean you might have to?

00:28.240 --> 00:30.196
If there's no earthquake
by Monday morning...

00:30.360 --> 00:31.793
...I have to write a book report.

00:31.960 --> 00:34.190
Oh, God. So, what's the book?

00:34.360 --> 00:36.669
William Shakespeare's
&lt;i>The Taming Of The Shrew.&lt;/i>

00:36.840 --> 00:38.831
By William Shakespeare.

00:39.800 --> 00:43.952
That'll come in handy when he's mopping
out the toilets at the House of Pancakes.

00:44.720 --> 00:47.154
You know,
I could go for some pancakes.

00:47.320 --> 00:49.197
Jake, please tell me you read the book.

00:49.880 --> 00:51.154
I really wish I could, Dad.

00:53.440 --> 00:55.271
I was gonna read it, but I can't find it.

00:55.440 --> 00:56.634
You lost the book?

00:56.800 --> 00:58.631
What do you intend to do
about the report?

00:58.800 --> 01:00.677
You mean aside from the earthquake?

01:02.040 --> 01:03.155
Yeah.

01:03.320 --> 01:06.437
Well, I kind of put all my eggs
in the earthquake basket.

01:06.840 --> 01:08.512
Get dressed. We're going to the store.

01:08.680 --> 01:10.352
- Well, can we stop for pancakes?
- Go.

01:12.680 --> 01:16.514
I bet you're sorry you took
all that LSD before you had him.

01:18.480 --> 01:19.879
I never took any LSD.

01:20.480 --> 01:22.755
You might wanna start
telling people you did.

01:32.080 --> 01:34.674
Unbelievable. You had four weeks
to write this book report.

01:34.840 --> 01:36.876
Get over it, Dad.

01:37.920 --> 01:38.909
Yeah, Alan. Relax.

01:39.080 --> 01:41.548
He'll have eight weeks
of summer school to do it.

01:42.040 --> 01:43.598
Unless there's an earthquake.

01:45.440 --> 01:48.591
Excuse me, could you tell me
where the classic literature section is?

01:48.760 --> 01:50.990
- Third floor near the restroom.
- Thank you.

01:51.160 --> 01:52.878
Go ahead. I'm gonna look at magazines.

01:53.040 --> 01:56.191
They don't sell those kinds of magazines
here. I checked.

01:57.560 --> 01:59.471
Come on, you little perv.
Meet me back here.

02:00.480 --> 02:03.358
Wait, was that an earthquake?

02:06.080 --> 02:07.798
Can I help you find anything?

02:07.960 --> 02:09.837
Yeah, I'm looking for a book.

02:12.920 --> 02:14.638
You probably need more than that.

02:14.800 --> 02:17.519
I want a book about,
you know, relationship stuff.

02:18.480 --> 02:20.277
Relationship stuff.

02:20.440 --> 02:24.558
No, not "relationship stuff,"
just relationship stuff.

02:24.920 --> 02:26.319
In the self-help section.

02:27.160 --> 02:29.833
- Thanks.
- Best of luck.

02:33.040 --> 02:35.270
This is worse than buying condoms.

02:36.920 --> 02:38.512
Okay, let's see.

02:38.680 --> 02:40.557
&lt;i>"Why Relationships Fail."&lt;/i>

02:41.480 --> 02:43.471
&lt;i>"Smart Women, Foolish Choices."&lt;/i>

02:44.160 --> 02:46.196
Thank God for those gals.

02:46.680 --> 02:48.272
- Excuse me.
- Sorry.

02:48.440 --> 02:49.998
Oh, &lt;i>"Embracing Your Soul Mate."&lt;/i>

02:50.840 --> 02:54.196
Oh, "soul mate."
I thought it was "cellmate."

02:55.640 --> 02:57.278
You know, a prison love story?

02:57.680 --> 02:58.669
I see.

02:59.000 --> 03:01.116
Not that I'm into prison love stories.

03:01.280 --> 03:02.793
I like the girls-in-prison stuff.

03:04.760 --> 03:06.830
Oh, who am I kidding?

03:07.320 --> 03:08.878
I'm looking for some help, okay?

03:09.560 --> 03:12.597
You're not alone. There are
millions of people looking for help.

03:12.760 --> 03:15.149
Gee, thanks for making me feel special.

03:16.520 --> 03:17.953
Let me ask you something.

03:18.120 --> 03:20.873
What would you change about yourself
if you could?

03:21.040 --> 03:23.349
- I don't know, little things, I guess.
- Like what?

03:24.040 --> 03:26.031
Well,
I guess I'd like to be a little happier.

03:26.200 --> 03:29.158
Maybe find a way to sustain
a healthy relationship with a woman...

03:29.320 --> 03:32.118
...so I don't,
you know, grow old and die alone...

03:32.280 --> 03:34.555
...incontinent and unloved.

03:35.640 --> 03:38.200
Yes, the little things.

03:38.360 --> 03:39.759
Can I recommend a book for you?

03:40.360 --> 03:41.509
Well, as long as I'm here.

03:47.560 --> 03:51.473
&lt;i>"Breaking Barriers:&lt;/i>
&lt;i>Finding The Intimacy You Deserve."&lt;/i>

03:51.640 --> 03:54.552
I don't know.
I was hoping to do better than I deserve.

03:54.720 --> 03:57.075
Give it a chance.
I hear it's helped a lot of people.

03:57.480 --> 03:59.516
For 25 bucks, it better wash my car.

04:03.000 --> 04:04.752
Wait a minute, is this you?

04:05.280 --> 04:06.952
Armor All's extra.

04:07.120 --> 04:10.635
- Cool. Will you sign it for me?
- Oh, I'd be happy to. What's your name?

04:10.800 --> 04:13.633
- Charlie.
- Okay.

04:13.960 --> 04:14.949
Great.

04:15.120 --> 04:18.351
Now, that it's autographed,
I'm not a loser, I'm a collector.

04:19.640 --> 04:21.198
Here you go.

04:22.560 --> 04:27.156
"To Charlie, reading a self-help book
doesn't make you less of a man."

04:27.880 --> 04:29.836
Okay, back to loser.

04:30.640 --> 04:31.629
You're not a loser.

04:31.800 --> 04:34.030
Like most men,
you're just afraid to be vulnerable.

04:34.200 --> 04:37.237
Excuse me, but what sane person
wants to be vulnerable?

04:37.880 --> 04:40.075
If you're not vulnerable,
you can't feel anything.

04:40.240 --> 04:41.832
Yeah, and?

04:42.680 --> 04:43.669
Read the book.

04:45.200 --> 04:46.792
Wait.

04:47.200 --> 04:48.633
Can I buy you a cup of coffee?

04:49.000 --> 04:51.275
- Why?
- I'd like to talk to you some more.

04:51.760 --> 04:53.637
Are you still gonna buy the book?

04:53.800 --> 04:56.155
I have to. You wrote all over it.

04:57.120 --> 04:58.872
- Then sure, why not?
- Great.

04:59.480 --> 05:01.436
If I give you the money,
will you pay for it?

05:01.600 --> 05:04.319
I don't need any more sympathy
from the help.

05:05.240 --> 05:06.514
What's a shrew anyway?

05:06.680 --> 05:08.238
Oh, it's a small rodent.

05:08.400 --> 05:10.197
Oh, so this is like &lt;i>Stuart Little?&lt;/i>

05:10.680 --> 05:14.639
No, no, it's about a man
trying to control a willful, angry woman.

05:14.800 --> 05:17.075
Is he trying to control her with rodents?

05:18.720 --> 05:20.278
I don't wanna spoil it for you.

05:20.840 --> 05:23.718
Let's just find your Uncle Charlie
and get out of here.

05:23.880 --> 05:28.237
Excuse me, have you seen a guy,
dark hair, bowling shirt, shorts?

05:28.400 --> 05:30.152
Oh, yeah, the self-help guy.

05:30.320 --> 05:31.833
No, that doesn't sound like him.

05:32.000 --> 05:34.355
A guy like that just left
with a pretty blond woman.

05:34.520 --> 05:36.476
That sounds like him.

05:37.080 --> 05:38.399
Dad, this is the wrong book.

05:38.960 --> 05:41.997
- What are you talking about?
- It's in some sort of foreign language.

05:42.160 --> 05:43.832
It's Elizabethan.

05:44.000 --> 05:45.752
Well, can we get one in English?

05:46.840 --> 05:48.512
Walk.

05:52.720 --> 05:55.029
How could you
have already lost the book?

05:55.200 --> 05:57.760
I didn't do it on purpose.
What are you yelling at me for?

05:57.920 --> 06:01.071
Because it's one of the few pleasures
of being your father.

06:02.680 --> 06:06.309
- Oh, look who's here. Thanks a lot.
- What did I do?

06:06.480 --> 06:08.755
You stranded us at the mall.
We had to take the bus.

06:08.920 --> 06:13.232
The bus, I left the book on the bus.
There, mystery solved.

06:14.200 --> 06:15.155
Go get in the car.

06:15.520 --> 06:18.193
- Where are we going?
- Where do you think we're going?

06:18.680 --> 06:21.240
Well, we never did get those pancakes.

06:22.360 --> 06:24.510
We're going to the bookstore
to buy another book.

06:24.680 --> 06:27.274
- This one's coming out of your allowance.
- What allowance?

06:29.880 --> 06:33.395
- I'm supposed to be getting an allowance?
- Go get your shoes.

06:39.000 --> 06:40.592
- Did you guys feel that?
- Move it.

06:44.960 --> 06:46.075
So guess what.

06:46.240 --> 06:49.550
I'm gonna transform my life
and get the intimacy I deserve.

06:50.080 --> 06:51.069
Fantastic.

06:51.240 --> 06:53.993
You work on that while
I go back to the mall with taterhead.

06:55.400 --> 06:58.312
Not only that,
I met the author and she's amazing.

06:58.480 --> 07:01.074
- The woman you dumped us for?
- Yeah, know what she told me?

07:01.240 --> 07:02.389
No idea.

07:02.560 --> 07:06.269
She told me that my fear of being hurt
keeps me from feeling anything at all.

07:06.440 --> 07:09.352
It's like I'm living in an emotional prison
that I built myself.

07:09.520 --> 07:11.954
How about that? You abandoned us.

07:12.560 --> 07:13.879
I know, but get this.

07:14.040 --> 07:16.474
I'm not just a prisoner, I'm the warden.

07:18.760 --> 07:21.957
We had to take two buses and walk a mile
on the Pacific Coast Highway...

07:22.120 --> 07:23.269
...during rush hour.

07:23.800 --> 07:25.791
I get it. I understand.

07:25.960 --> 07:29.555
But the good news is
I hold the keys to my own freedom.

07:30.400 --> 07:33.551
There's no sidewalk
on the Pacific Coast highway.

07:34.760 --> 07:36.716
Okay, okay, I hear you.

07:36.880 --> 07:38.359
You're angry and resentful.

07:38.520 --> 07:40.112
But what you need to understand...

07:40.280 --> 07:43.955
...is that resentment is the mortar that
holds the bricks of Ioneliness together...

07:44.120 --> 07:46.031
...in a wall of alienation and despair.

07:48.000 --> 07:50.958
Chapter 3, "Knocking Down the Wall."

07:51.960 --> 07:53.518
Bite me.

07:55.120 --> 07:58.669
That's Chapter 1 in my forthcoming book
entitled &lt;i>Bite Me.&lt;/i>

08:00.440 --> 08:03.113
Chapter 2 is called,
"Kiss My Pale White Ass."

08:04.920 --> 08:07.195
- We can't go back to the mall.
- Why not?

08:07.360 --> 08:08.759
My shoes are missing.

08:12.600 --> 08:14.033
Another mystery solved.

08:16.600 --> 08:17.589
Wrong foot, buddy.

08:19.720 --> 08:20.709
Oh, yeah, thanks.

08:22.160 --> 08:24.151
Guess I should be reading
&lt;i>Taming of the Shoe.&lt;/i>

08:26.560 --> 08:27.959
Get it?

08:30.120 --> 08:33.032
You might wanna start thinking
about having him neutered.

08:38.800 --> 08:40.279
This is delicious.

08:40.440 --> 08:42.192
I've never had Ethiopian food before.

08:43.160 --> 08:45.196
I've loved it
ever since I lived in Ethiopia.

08:46.400 --> 08:47.958
When did you live there?

08:48.440 --> 08:49.759
Let's see.

08:49.920 --> 08:51.638
It would have to be 1972.

08:52.600 --> 08:55.273
1972? Were you born there?

08:56.480 --> 09:00.075
Don't be silly. This was right after college.
I was in the Peace Corps.

09:02.040 --> 09:05.032
College, 1972.

09:05.560 --> 09:06.549
Need a pencil?

09:08.200 --> 09:09.872
No, no, no.

09:10.040 --> 09:13.396
I was just thinking
what I was doing in 1972.

09:13.560 --> 09:14.788
Oh, tell me.

09:15.920 --> 09:17.512
I don't have a vivid memory of it...

09:17.680 --> 09:20.797
...but I'm sure that's the year
I graduated to the big-boy potty.

09:22.920 --> 09:24.478
It was quite a year for both of us.

09:27.040 --> 09:29.429
So are you still using
that college degree?

09:29.600 --> 09:32.114
Because I'm still using
the big-boy potty.

09:33.600 --> 09:36.398
You're used to going out
with younger women, aren't you?

09:36.840 --> 09:40.913
Well, I don't really think about age
as much as I think about personality...

09:41.080 --> 09:46.313
...and, you know,
chemistry and education, family values.

09:48.480 --> 09:50.835
All right, young and dumb,
you got me.

09:52.760 --> 09:56.116
I'm not judging you, Charlie. You're a man
and you know what you want.

09:56.280 --> 09:58.111
What's wrong with that?

09:58.920 --> 10:00.239
Nothing?

10:00.600 --> 10:01.828
Nothing.

10:02.000 --> 10:04.230
You are fine just the way you are.

10:05.200 --> 10:07.919
- I am?
- Of course, you are.

10:09.920 --> 10:12.593
If I called my mother now,
would you tell her that?

10:13.680 --> 10:15.159
You don't think she knows?

10:15.320 --> 10:16.594
As far as she's concerned...

10:16.760 --> 10:19.797
...the last thing I did right
was evacuate her uterus.

10:19.960 --> 10:22.793
Oh, you poor thing. That's awful.

10:22.960 --> 10:24.234
It is, isn't it?

10:24.600 --> 10:27.353
Every little boy
needs to feel loved and nurtured.

10:27.520 --> 10:31.672
Otherwise, he grows up with a hole
inside him that he can never fill.

10:31.840 --> 10:34.991
Oh, I have got such a big hole.

10:35.160 --> 10:37.310
If my hole could talk.

10:39.040 --> 10:40.871
You've got a little something
right here.

10:43.760 --> 10:45.398
I'll get it.

10:48.640 --> 10:50.471
- There we go.
- Thanks.

10:51.280 --> 10:52.554
You know what?

10:53.400 --> 10:54.469
I like you.

10:55.240 --> 10:57.708
Well, I like you too, Charlie.

11:00.600 --> 11:02.033
Try the Yemiser Kik Wat.

11:03.880 --> 11:05.074
Looks kind of yucky.

11:05.560 --> 11:07.596
Well, don't look at it. Just taste it.

11:08.920 --> 11:11.309
Oh, come on, just one bite. For me?

11:15.600 --> 11:17.113
Okay.

11:22.680 --> 11:24.113
Hey, it's good.

11:24.280 --> 11:25.679
I told you.

11:25.840 --> 11:28.718
Oh, excuse me.
Could I get another napkin?

11:33.240 --> 11:35.231
So, what do they have for dessert?

11:38.680 --> 11:41.638
Well, Charlie,
thank you for a lovely evening.

11:41.800 --> 11:43.552
You're welcome.

11:46.360 --> 11:48.920
Can I kiss you good night?

11:49.480 --> 11:51.948
Do you usually ask permission?

11:52.480 --> 11:53.879
Well, no.

11:54.520 --> 11:56.397
Then why are you asking now?

11:57.000 --> 11:59.958
I don't know.
I don't wanna get in trouble.

12:08.040 --> 12:09.189
Okay, I'm in trouble.

12:13.400 --> 12:15.311
Oh, I'm sorry.
I thought I heard something.

12:15.480 --> 12:17.038
It's okay. Jeremy, this is Charlie.

12:17.200 --> 12:19.430
- Charlie, this is my son, Jeremy.
- Hey, man.

12:19.600 --> 12:21.033
- How are you?
- How's it going?

12:21.200 --> 12:23.998
I didn't mean to interrupt.
I dropped in to fix your computer.

12:24.160 --> 12:26.469
I'll leave you two alone.
Charlie, good meeting you.

12:26.640 --> 12:28.039
Same here.

12:30.040 --> 12:31.632
So that's your son?

12:33.000 --> 12:34.672
- How old is he?
- Thirty-two.

12:36.680 --> 12:37.999
They're cute at that age.

12:57.560 --> 12:59.551
- Hey.
- What?

12:59.720 --> 13:01.915
You're supposed
to be finishing your report.

13:02.080 --> 13:04.275
I know, but I can't find the book.

13:07.120 --> 13:09.315
You're kidding. We just bought it.

13:09.480 --> 13:10.595
What can I say, Dad?

13:10.760 --> 13:12.910
It's a big house and a little book.

13:14.080 --> 13:16.514
Find the book.

13:17.080 --> 13:20.436
- I'm really tired.
- Find the book.

13:21.960 --> 13:23.951
Just saying it won't make it happen.

13:26.040 --> 13:29.476
Find the book!

13:31.720 --> 13:32.914
Heads up. He's losing it.

13:34.080 --> 13:35.991
I should have put frosting
on the damn book.

13:36.160 --> 13:38.515
He's never lost anything
with frosting on it.

13:39.160 --> 13:42.038
I don't know why you continue
to bang your head against the wall.

13:42.200 --> 13:45.875
The kid's obviously destined to sell
tube socks out of the trunk of his car.

13:47.480 --> 13:49.835
A business of his own.

13:50.000 --> 13:52.116
Gee, that'd be swell.

13:53.960 --> 13:57.748
- So how was your date?
- Terrific.

13:57.920 --> 14:01.708
- Then why are you home so early?
- Well, turns out she has a kid.

14:01.880 --> 14:02.995
Single mom, huh?

14:03.920 --> 14:05.399
Yeah.

14:06.360 --> 14:08.590
That's what she is, single mom.

14:08.760 --> 14:10.512
- How old?
- Thirty-two.

14:10.680 --> 14:12.910
- I meant the kid.
- So did I.

14:13.400 --> 14:14.355
You're kidding.

14:14.520 --> 14:16.909
If she's got a 32-year-old kid
that would make her...

14:17.080 --> 14:18.798
Don't do the math, please.

14:18.960 --> 14:20.791
It all goes south
when you do the math.

14:21.560 --> 14:24.358
Come on, so you're dating
an older woman. It's no big deal.

14:24.520 --> 14:26.715
That's it?
You're not gonna give me a hard time?

14:26.880 --> 14:28.916
Don't be silly.
I'm more evolved than that.

14:29.560 --> 14:30.993
Well, good.

14:32.040 --> 14:35.316
&lt;i>Just a gigolo&lt;/i>
&lt;i>Everywhere I go&lt;/i>

14:35.480 --> 14:39.029
&lt;i>People know the part&lt;/i>
&lt;i>I'm playing&lt;/i>

14:39.640 --> 14:41.312
I guess I'm not.

14:42.360 --> 14:44.112
Look, this is a spectacular woman...

14:44.280 --> 14:46.669
...and it doesn't matter in the least
how old she is.

14:46.840 --> 14:49.559
Please. You can't even tolerate age spots
on a banana.

14:50.920 --> 14:56.916
Okay, okay, first of all, on a banana,
spots are an indication of mushiness.

14:57.080 --> 15:01.232
And second,
I haven't peeled this woman yet.

15:08.440 --> 15:09.873
In the freezer?

15:10.880 --> 15:13.997
- Jake.
- I found it, I'm reading.

15:14.160 --> 15:16.116
It's really cool.

15:28.840 --> 15:31.798
- For God's sake.
- Hey, I was reading that.

15:31.960 --> 15:34.269
You're writing a report
on &lt;i>The Taming of The Shrew...&lt;/i>

15:34.440 --> 15:36.112
...not the voyages of Cap'n Crunch.

15:36.440 --> 15:39.000
Too bad.
I could write the crap out of that.

15:41.880 --> 15:46.158
Okay, I'm not fooling around here.

15:46.320 --> 15:49.995
You're gonna finish this damn book
and write the damn report...

15:50.160 --> 15:52.390
...you're gonna hand it in Monday,
spell-checked...

15:52.560 --> 15:55.154
...formatted and on freaking time.

15:56.000 --> 15:58.195
I have my doubts, Dad.

16:00.080 --> 16:02.674
- Read.
- Fine.

16:05.880 --> 16:06.869
Listen to this.

16:07.040 --> 16:08.792
"A sleeve? 'Tis like a demi-cannon:

16:08.960 --> 16:11.952
What! Up and down,
carv'd like an apple-tart?"

16:12.120 --> 16:14.680
All I get from this is
"blah, blah, blah, apple tart."

16:16.520 --> 16:18.351
Have we got any apple tarts?

16:22.040 --> 16:23.837
- Hi.
- Hi.

16:27.200 --> 16:28.189
Good.

16:28.360 --> 16:30.999
I was afraid that first kiss
might have been a fluke.

16:31.160 --> 16:33.913
Well, I don't know about you,
but that was not my first kiss.

16:34.320 --> 16:35.833
Come on in.

16:36.400 --> 16:38.356
Wow, what a beautiful home.

16:39.240 --> 16:40.798
Thank you.

16:42.840 --> 16:44.512
How much of it do you wanna see?

16:47.680 --> 16:49.636
This'll be enough for today.

16:50.280 --> 16:51.952
Understood. Let's hit the road.

16:52.120 --> 16:53.758
Aren't you gonna take a jacket?

16:53.920 --> 16:55.035
I'm okay, don't need one.

16:55.200 --> 16:58.351
- It gets cool in Santa Barbara, Charlie.
- I'll be fine.

16:58.520 --> 17:01.671
Please. If you don't need it,
you can leave it in the car.

17:02.560 --> 17:04.039
All right.

17:05.320 --> 17:08.073
- Take a look around.
- Thanks, I will.

17:09.120 --> 17:11.953
Oh, hi, you must be Angie.

17:12.120 --> 17:13.712
I'm Alan, Charlie's brother.

17:13.880 --> 17:15.950
Oh, of course, hi.
Oh, what a firm handshake.

17:16.120 --> 17:19.032
Oh, well, no one trusts
a chiropractor with limp hands.

17:19.200 --> 17:20.428
Oh, you're a chiropractor?

17:21.080 --> 17:23.310
Hang on.
I could have gotten into medical school.

17:23.480 --> 17:25.755
I didn't wanna spend
four years in South America.

17:25.920 --> 17:29.276
- No, no, I'm a big fan of chiropractics.
- You're kidding.

17:29.440 --> 17:31.635
No, I think you people
are miracle workers.

17:32.320 --> 17:33.878
Okay, I'm ready to go.

17:34.560 --> 17:36.596
Did you put on sun block?

17:36.920 --> 17:37.955
I don't need sun block.

17:38.120 --> 17:39.872
Oh, honey, I think you do.

17:40.040 --> 17:42.838
You have beautiful skin.
I don't wanna see it get burned.

17:43.000 --> 17:44.911
You're right, thanks.

17:45.480 --> 17:50.679
So anyway, you were saying something
about me being a miracle worker?

17:50.840 --> 17:53.195
Oh, God, yes.
I threw my back out last year skiing.

17:53.360 --> 17:57.069
- My chiropractor just about saved my life.
- That's what we do, you know.

17:57.240 --> 18:00.437
We're not flashy, we don't get,
you know, special license plates...

18:00.600 --> 18:02.716
...so we can park
wherever the hell we want.

18:02.880 --> 18:04.996
You know,
nobody makes TV shows about us.

18:05.160 --> 18:09.756
Or calls us McDreamy
or McSteamy or McMuffin.

18:11.480 --> 18:13.710
We just quietly go about
the business of healing.

18:13.880 --> 18:15.552
- I know, I know.
- Thank you, thank you.

18:15.720 --> 18:17.631
I only wish more people appreciated us.

18:18.040 --> 18:19.837
You can't worry about
what people think.

18:20.000 --> 18:23.151
I know, but the lack of respect
really hurts, you know.

18:23.320 --> 18:27.472
Back-cracker, spine-cruncher,
quack, charlatan, witch doctor...

18:27.640 --> 18:29.995
- Alan.
...voodoo priest, fraud, failure.

18:30.160 --> 18:31.798
Hey, hey.

18:32.480 --> 18:34.516
Know what we call people
who say those things?

18:34.680 --> 18:35.795
My family?

18:36.600 --> 18:37.794
We call them damaged.

18:37.960 --> 18:40.520
They need to hurt others
to feel better about themselves.

18:40.680 --> 18:43.114
Exactly, the reason
I don't feel better about myself...

18:43.280 --> 18:45.555
...is I'm not good enough
at hurting them back.

18:46.000 --> 18:47.672
Oh, no, you don't wanna do that.

18:48.040 --> 18:49.871
Yeah, I kind of do.

18:50.240 --> 18:54.677
Alan, you need to ignore the negativity
and open yourself up...

18:54.840 --> 18:57.115
...to the nurturing love
that's all around you.

18:57.600 --> 18:59.955
- Love is all around me?
- Yes.

19:00.120 --> 19:02.998
Is it hiding
behind the loathing and rejection?

19:03.640 --> 19:06.677
Honey, I am loving you right now.

19:07.360 --> 19:09.794
- Really?
- Yes, really.

19:11.480 --> 19:12.799
Thank you.

19:16.720 --> 19:19.393
You are a wonderful,
valuable human being.

19:19.960 --> 19:21.598
I am?

19:22.120 --> 19:23.633
Yes, you are.

19:30.680 --> 19:32.989
I see you're getting to know
my brother.

19:40.440 --> 19:41.919
Isn't this beautiful country?

19:42.560 --> 19:44.835
Yeah, it's swell.

19:45.280 --> 19:48.955
Angie, if you like antiquing,
I know some great little shops.

19:49.120 --> 19:51.475
- I'm not going antiquing.
- Oh, that's okay.

19:51.640 --> 19:54.712
Angie and I will peel off
and you can sit in the park and drink.

19:55.840 --> 19:57.796
Are there any game arcades
in Santa Barbara?

19:57.960 --> 19:59.996
You won't have time.
You have a book to read.

20:00.160 --> 20:01.878
Oh, yeah.

20:02.280 --> 20:04.157
I forgot it.

20:04.880 --> 20:06.677
That's okay.
We can stop at a bookstore.

20:06.840 --> 20:08.990
Oh, gee,
we don't want to ruin your afternoon.

20:09.160 --> 20:11.310
Hey, we invited you.
We want you with us.

20:11.480 --> 20:13.436
- Right, Charlie?
- No.

20:13.600 --> 20:15.716
Oh, don't be that way.

20:16.160 --> 20:19.357
I tell you what, after we get Jake's book,
we'll stop and get ice cream.

20:19.520 --> 20:20.999
Yes.

20:51.040 --> 20:53.031
Subtitles by
SDI Media Group

20:53.200 --> 20:55.191
[ENGLISH]
